Closed System Transfer Devices are specialized medical devices designed to prevent hazardous drugs and vapors from escaping into the surrounding environment during medication preparation and administration. They also help protect medications from contamination by limiting the entry of external contaminants into the drug-transfer pathway.

These devices are particularly important in oncology pharmacies, hospital compounding units, and healthcare facilities that handle cytotoxic and other potentially hazardous drugs. Growing attention to occupational exposure risks and medication-handling procedures is encouraging healthcare providers to strengthen safety protocols and adopt closed-system technologies.

